The /catalogs/ link forms of page dialect 1 (docs-kit C11, docs mode). docs-kit
is the source of this case and of lint/clean/: both are byte-identical to
docs-kit internal/dialect/testdata/conformance/{link-catalogs,clean}/ at the
tag v0.2.2, the opm-docs release site/Dockerfile pins (expect here equals
shell.out there). The accepted /catalogs/ forms are this case's line 7 and its
reference definition; docs-kit's clean case carries none. A bump of the
opm-docs pin re-syncs every case that changed in the conformance set at the
new tag, in the same PR, and names that tag here.

test-site.sh runs both linters over every case. The slashless minor, edge and
root links are the cases link-slashless-minor, link-slashless-edge and
link-slashless-root, synced from the same tag; since opm-docs 0.2.1 both
linters name the same rule for them.
